      "message": "ConvertBuffer_8bppPlt2Gray() only has 1 caller: ConvertBuffer_8bppMask(). There, one can see there has to be a palette. From the name, and from the only caller to ConvertBuffer_8bppMask(), one can see the GetBpp() value is 8.\n\nSeparately, in CFX_DIBBase::BuildPalette(), it builds a palette of size 256 when the BPP is 8.\n\nOne can take this code and remove the UNSAFE_TODO() to see what the compiler is complaining about. I believe it\u0027s actually accessing `gray` that is unsafe, because `gray` is a C-array, whose operator[] does not check bounds. Whereas `src_palette` is a pdfium::span, and pdfium::span::operator[] does check.",
